iPet
https://github.com/xufilps/iPet

This project is derived from VPet / VPet-Simulator by LorisYounger and
its contributors: https://github.com/LorisYounger/VPet
Original source baseline: 1a06c5981330564bab05a098d2d7969a4b119dd3.
Original authorship, copyright notices and Git history are retained; upstream source remains available in that history and at the upstream repository.

Modifications by the iPet project (2026-10-01): added a native Swift
implementation for macOS, reusable pet simulation and SpriteKit rendering
modules, asset-conversion/build/test tooling, and iPet documentation/branding.
The original C# implementation is retained in Git history, not the current source tree. The original README and translations remain available in Git history and at the fixed upstream baseline; the current README documents iPet.
Code continues to be distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0;
the original LICENSE is included unchanged.

iPet is a derivative adaptation and is not presented as the original author's
release or as an official Apple-platform release of VPet.

IMPORTANT: The Apache code license does not replace the separate authorization
for bundled pet animations and images. The original pet animation/image rights
belong to the VUP-Simulator production team (虚拟主播模拟器制作组).
See Apple/ANIMATION_LICENSE.md and Apple/ATTRIBUTION.md for their original terms,
source attribution and distribution requirements. Those notices accompany the
application together with this NOTICE and LICENSE. No fee is charged for the
redistribution of animation files in this source repository.

The iPet pixel-style application icon was generated with OpenAI imagegen using the original vpeticon.png as a visual reference. This does not change the original character and animation licensing. See Apple/Design/README.md and Apple/ATTRIBUTION.md.

The original C# project files were removed from the current iPet source tree; the upstream project remains at https://github.com/LorisYounger/VPet. Required original animation/configuration assets, attribution, licenses and Git history are retained.

The native legacy LPS compatibility decoder follows the serialization contracts
of LinePutScript 1.11.9 by LorisYounger (LB Copyright © 2018), licensed under
Apache-2.0: https://github.com/LorisYounger/LinePutScript/tree/69ea42f7f213be2669879705035a77a1804c457a .
The Swift implementation is modified for bounded parsing and explicit numeric
rejection. A development-only fixture generator uses the original NuGet library;
the macOS application does not bundle or require the .NET library.

Repository layout update (2026-10-03): unchanged upstream assets moved to Assets/Upstream/VPet/Core; original Windows documentation and configuration archived byte-for-byte in docs/upstream. Native app sources moved to Apple/Apps/macOS. Current Swift and community development guidance replaces the root Windows-specific contribution/configuration entries.

Documentation cleanup (2026-10-03): replaced the root README with current iPet guidance and removed duplicate upstream README translations and redirect files. Original code license, authorship, applicable notices and animation authorization are retained.
